<title>GERMANY: BMW says 1997 H1 profit, sales higher.</title>
<headline>BMW says 1997 H1 profit, sales higher.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30,</p>
<p>1997 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   435     vs 335</p>
<p>    Group sales				  29,100  vs 25,200</p>
<p>    Car production (units)		   625,450 vs 575,165</p>
<p>    --of which BMW branded cars	    350,778 vs 318,625</p>
<p>    --of which Rover branded cars	  250,382 vs 238,154</p>
<p>    Group deliveries (units)		 601,070 vs 556,779</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Bayerische Motoren-Werke AG. BMW took over Rover Group in 1994.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
